{
  "requirement": "A definition glob MUST match a complete full name. `*` MUST match zero or more characters, including dots; all other valid name characters MUST match literally. An empty glob MUST be invalid. Every definition selection MUST use this matching rule, including requirements evidence inputs, CLI definition filters, and the authoring `references` tool, and MUST match against both requirements and named examples.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the sources satisfy `requirements.references.definition_globs`.**\n\n**Implementation**\n\n- `src/definition_glob.rs` `matches`:\n  - It is a full-string dynamic-programming matcher over the whole name, so it matches a complete full name and never a prefix or substring.\n  - `*` matches zero or more bytes, including `.`.\n  - Every other byte must equal the name byte, so it matches literally.\n- `src/definition_glob.rs` `validate`:\n  - It rejects the empty glob.\n  - It also rejects any character outside the valid name characters (alphanumerics, `.`, `_`, `-`) and `*`. That agrees with `valid_name` in `src/lib.rs`, so \"all other valid name characters\" are the only literals a glob can contain.\n- Every definition selection named in the requirement uses these two functions:\n  - **Requirements evidence inputs:** `InputSelector::resolve` in `src/inputs.rs` validates the glob, filters with `matches`, and errors when nothing matches. `add-input --requirements` and `validate_resolved_input` in `src/evidence.rs` go through it. The authoring `source_input` in `src/authoring/inputs.rs` applies the same matcher.\n  - **CLI definition filters:** `status_markdown_with_options` and `info_markdown` in `src/commands.rs` validate the glob, report \"no definitions match\" when nothing matches, and filter with `matches`.\n  - **Authoring `references` tool:** `references` in `src/authoring/tools.rs` validates the selection and uses `matches` for the definitions list, the reference sites, and the anchor sites.\n- All of these select requirements and named examples and skip `DefinitionKind::Term`, as the requirement says.\n- Each of these functions carries an `{impl}` reference. I found no other glob-matching code that lacks one.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- The unit test `wildcard_crosses_dot_segments_and_matches_the_whole_name` in `src/definition_glob.rs` covers:\n  - `*` crossing dots;\n  - rejection of a match that has an extra prefix (`prefix.foo.x.bar`);\n  - a missing required `.` (`foo.bar.*` does not match `foo.bar`);\n  - an empty glob being invalid;\n  - an invalid character (`[`) being rejected.\n- `requirements_inputs_track_matched_declarations_in_full_name_order` in `src/evidence.rs` tests the example `definition_glob_cases`. It shows `foo.*.bar` matching both a requirement and a named example in full-name order, and it covers added, removed, and changed matches and the no-match error.\n- `commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors` in `tests/commands.rs` covers:\n  - an invalid glob (`[`) for both `info` and `status`;\n  - an unmatched glob;\n  - `requirements.*ready` matching `requirements.ready` (zero characters) and `requirements.xready`, while excluding `requirements.pending`.\n- Further tests cover requirements and examples being selected together and named definitions being excluded:\n  - `definition_glob_lists_a_requirement_and_an_example_in_info_and_status`;\n  - `selections_match_requirements_and_examples_but_never_named_definitions`;\n  - the `add-input` tests.\n- `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` in `src/authoring/tools.rs` exercises the authoring `references` tool with an exact name, `requirements.*`, a missing name, `bad name`, and an empty selection. It is marked as a test for `authoring.reference_index` rather than this requirement, but it does cover the behavior.\n\n**Minor gaps**\n\n- There is no test that `.`, `_`, or `-` in a glob are literal rather than wildcards.\n- The authoring `references` tool's glob test is not marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n\nNeither gap is a failure of the stated obligations, and the implementation is simple and clearly correct.",
  "references": "68bc1f3b56298f1e9ddb0a76d85acf729bb450e21baaf8f31b3f08101f8bbd24",
